    Why? T_block=2.6ms is 2.6× larger than the 1ms synthetic value.
    Larger T_block → larger T_compute → larger absolute bubble cost.
    The bubble fraction (pp-1)/M = 3/4 = 75% of one pass is the same,
    but the absolute cost scales with T_block.

    Despite this, pp=4 tp=2 dp=1 still wins because the alternative:
      pp=2 tp=2 dp=2 → adds DP AllReduce (cross-node gradient sync) ~90ms
      pp=8 tp=1 dp=1 → 8 stages, bubble = 7/4 × compute = huge bubble
    Eliminating DP sync (from ~90ms to 0ms) is a far bigger win than any
    other optimization on this cluster.

  ↳ Why pp=4 tp=2 dp=1 still wins vs pp=4 tp=1 dp=2?
    pp=4 tp=1 dp=2 has DP AllReduce over cross-node pairs (~75ms).
    pp=4 tp=2 dp=1 has NO DP AllReduce (dp=1). The TP overhead (1.8ms intra-node)
    is negligible compared to eliminating 75ms of cross-node gradient sync.

